 Garrison  Garrison 
                    
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing tall with his warriors was Kahn.  No generals were present to 
lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  An unfavorable omen appeared, which of course dealt a severe blow to Kahn
's hopes.  It seems that Kahn's mount was shot down while Kahn was giving a 
speech.  As the battle intensified, the tactical abilities of the acting 
commander and Kahn appeared evenly matched and neither general could gain a 
tactical advantage.

  Out on the left outside wing, the 218th Legion were aided in the battle by 
a band of medicine men sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which aroused 
them to a fanatical zeal.  They were arrayed against the 121st Garrison.  
The 220th Light Cavalry outflanked the enemy lines and charged in with full 
strength.  On this battleground, the 218th Legion audaciously charged their 
enemy, but became disordered and were thrown back by a well-timed, sustained 
countercharge.  Even so, the 218th Legion battled with the 121st Garrison 
and gradually shoved them back.
  Out on the right outside wing, the 188th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
153rd Garrison.  In this area, the men of the 153rd Garrison encountered 
unpredictable footing and experienced confusion.  The 188th Bowmen fought 
with the 153rd Garrison and the fighting here proved inconclusive.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Uga-Buga Makumb, a 
final savage thrust defeated their enemy and won the day for Kahn.  The 
218th Legion scattered the 121st Garrison in all directions.  The 188th 
Bowmen chased after the enemy and annihilated the 153rd Garrison.
  Kahn's host concluded the campaign successfully and conquered the province 
of Bronzeleaf.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we could not 
have been more pleased with the elan of the 218th Legion, and we have 
elevated its rating to Veteran.  The 220th Light Cavalry fought determinedly 
during the battle and came through with a good effort.  We can now rank it a 
Veteran unit.  The acting commander withdrew to the Callisto Sea, defeated 
but not broken.
  In late summer, Kahn worked hard on his Tactics but was thwarted in his 
efforts.
  With the advent of the fall season, Kahn tried hard to improve his Tactics,
but he practiced in vain.
  The fall darkened into a frigid early winter.  Kahn attempted an illegal 
move.  He was ordered to move from Bronzeleaf to Sherwood, further than his 
army could move.  Instead, he studied and practiced his Archery and his 
skill in Archery went up.


  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Quantara Roo, a 
Plain area ruled by Kahn.  Quantara Roo was conquered and occupied by Guerin 
(#18)'s host.  Guerin leads approximately 4 Bowmen, 2 Heavy Cavalry, 1 Warg 
Riders, 2 Dragons and 1 Eagles.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Kahn (whose alliances are 
too incompatible) and Giovanna d'Arco (#7), degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  Kahn was visited by a hero from Valhalla, named Lancelot!  The 
characteristics for this great King from Game 32 are given in your 
"CHARACTERS" report.
  If Lancelot searches a feature, any monetary treasure Lancelot captures 
will be given to you.  If Lancelot captures a magic treasure, Lancelot will 
give it to your King when he departs for Valhalla, or you can order Lancelot 
to Give it to one of your characters.  You can do anything you want with the 
magic item Lancelot came with, but the item will leave at the end of her 
stay with you.  Except for the rules given in this paragraph, Lancelot can 
generally be treated just like your other Heroes, and can be affected by any 
spell except Resurrection.  The main limitation in using Lancelot is that 
Lancelot has only enough patience to practice with you for one of the 
phase(s) Lancelot is with you.  Lancelot will leave at the end of the last 
phase Lancelot is scheduled to serve you, after all battles have been 
fought.  Lancelot can lead armies, but when Lancelot returns to Valhalla, 
the armies will normally be left leaderless in the province they are in.  If 
Lancelot has the armies in a province you don't own, they will be 
transferred to your lowest-numbered leader in the same province, or at last 
resort, the garrison commander in an adjacent province owned by you.  If no 
leader is available, the armies will be disbanded.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Kahn for this year.


  Kahn treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Kahn treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn 
treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn asked Giovanna d'Arco (#7) to 
improve diplomatic relations with his great Kingdom, speaking at length of 
the great benefits of such an agreement.  The offer was graciously accepted 
by Giovanna d'Arco.
  Kahn treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Kahn's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 27 gold in revenue.  5 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 52nd Bowmen and the 68th Bowmen trained well and improved in quality.  
11 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Kahn was left with 23 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tonto, Squire to Hume
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Hume prepared to quench her thirst 
for glory.  She rode into Transylvania.  East of here lies the province of 
Big Sky (#306), ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  It is known to 
be a Mountain province inhabited by Dwarves.  Their Dwarven fighters fight 
as Axemen.  Viewing the southeastern horizon, one can see a poor Plain 
province called Kaluga (#307).  It is said that 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns there.  It is known to be populated 
by Elves.  Their Elven fighters traditionally array themselves in the style 
of Bowmen.  To the southwest there is a Mountain province known as Kiska 
(#207), a rich land of Eagles where Bradipo I rules.  They can call on an 
army of Eagles to defend their territory.  Hume encountered no wandering 
monster.
  The wet spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  Brunhilda (#86) 
informed Hume that Brunhilda would not sell her services for less than 4 
gold.
  In late summer, Hume practiced her Necromancy well but could not improve 
her Necromancy.
  With the advent of the fall season Hume travelled to Macondo.  During her 
travels this season, Hume was confronted by a Chimera.  Hoping to escape 
from her vicious opponent, Hume ran like the wind.  But she was too tired 
and, even with great effort, could not gain any ground on the Chimera.
  The Chimera moved to bow range.  The Chimera breathed a flame breath at 
Hume and missed.  The Chimera breathed a flame breath at Hume but his 
flame breath whiffed through the air.  Weaving her artful words of magic 
into a mighty Spiritwrack spell, Hume gestured with her arms, to make 
the Chimera quake and shiver with spiritual convulsions.  Incanting an 
Invisibility spell, Hume channelled scintillating, writhing strands of magic,
fading into invisibility.
  The Chimera charged into the melee.  The Chimera snapped at Hume and 
inflicted 2 damage points on her.  Hume thought to attempt a Fireball spell, 
but couldn't find a needed material component before Hume could make her 
spellcast.  The Chimera daringly snapped at Hume but Hume evaded the blow.  
Her spell was disrupted by the event.
  The Chimera then lunged at Hume and damaged her, inflicting 1 damage 
points.  Hume immediately thrust at the Chimera but her aim was just off.  
The Chimera treacherously snapped at Hume and inflicted 6 damage points.  
Showing no fear, Hume swang at the Chimera and scored on the Chimera, 
inflicting 4 points of damage.  Hume maneuvered for a better attacking 
position.  Then Hume swang at the Chimera and walloped the Chimera with 5 
damage points.  The Chimera pretended to panic, then pivoted and arrogantly 
snapped at Hume and inflicted 3 damage points on her.  Hume dropped to the 
ground, mortally pierced.  And so it came to pass that Hume met her unseemly 
end.


  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Hume


From: Charious
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I travelled in search of Kahn.  I journeyed to Quantara Roo.  I 
caught up with Kahn in Quantara Roo.  I scouted for Kahn in the province of 
Quantara Roo.  I encountered Kahn.  I talked to Kahn.  In my travels, I saw 
no marauding monsters.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  I could not cast Resurrection 
on Kahn because Kahn was in another province.  Instead, I tried to practice 
my Sageness, but the task was beyond my aptitude.  I invented nothing worthy 
of note in my sagely researches.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I could not cast 
Resurrection on Kahn because Kahn was in another province.  Instead, I 
practiced my Archery well but could not improve my Archery.
  With the advent of the fall season, I could not cast Resurrection on Kahn 
because Kahn was in another province.  Instead, I discovered nothing worthy 
of note in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I could not cast Resurrection 
on Kahn because Kahn was in another province.  Instead, I practiced my 
Archery diligently for many weeks, but could make no progress.

  Thy humble servant,   Charious


From: Hawkins
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I travelled to Gnarlia.
  During early summer, I recruited the 52nd Bowmen and the 68th Bowmen from 
among the people of Gnarlia, to serve under me.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer arrived.  I cast a spell giving 
magical powers of oratory to me.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  I moved into Peachwood (#1202) with my 
redoubtable army.

  Kahn's forces initiated a campaign of conquest directed at Peachwood, a 
Forest province owing allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1). 
Hawkins's forces experienced little resistance in Peachwood and I there 
established our reign.  Peachwood was discovered to have an income of 6 
gold.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  I marched on Bronzeleaf (#1303) with 
my command.

  Thy humble servant,   Hawkins


From: Tonto, Squire to Fingol
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Fingol rode into Bronzeleaf.  While adventuring, he encountered 
no monster.
  With the advent of the early summer season Fingol travelled to the 
Callisto Sea.  Viewing the southeastern horizon, one can see a Forest 
province known as the Falkland Sea (#1305).  It is said that 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll is the ruler there.  It is known to be 
occupied by Elves.  Their Elven warriors fight in the style of Bowmen and 
Fleet.  To the southwest there is a Jungle province known as Kumasi (#1205), 
a poor land of Trolls where Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns.  They 
can muster an army of Trolls to defend their territory.  West of here is 
Mare Ionium (#1104), a prosperous Sea province owned by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll, where no races dwell.  While 
adventuring, Fingol encountered no monster.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer came.  Fingol journeyed to Mare 
Ionium.  Turning to the southwest, one can see a rich Forest area, which is 
known as the Jellyfish Sea (#1105).  It is populated by Dwarves and 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll rules there.  Their Dwarven warriors 
prefer to fight in the style of Axemen and Fleet.  To the west lies a Forest 
area called Kildare (#1004), populated by Elves.  It is ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Their Elven warriors fight as Legion 
and Chariots.  Northwest of here lies the prosperous province of the Angel 
Sea (#1103), ruled by no one.  It is said to be a Sea province inhabited by 
Whales.  They can muster an army of Whales to defend their territory.  
Fingol encountered no marauding monsters.
  In fall, Fingol moved into Kildare.  Viewing the southwestern horizon, one 
can see a Forest province known as the Virgo Sea (#1005).  It is said that 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns there.  It is known to be 
populated by Elves.  Their Elven fighters prefer to array themselves in the 
style of Axemen and Heavy Cavalry.  To the west there lies a Sea province 
known as the Sixth Sea (#904), a prosperous area of Whales where no one 
rules.  They can muster a host of Whales to defend their territory.  
Northwest of here is the Crabman Sea (#1003), a Sea province owned by no one,
where no races dwell.  In his travels, Fingol encountered no marauding 
monsters.
  With the advent of the early winter season Fingol relieved Fingol of his 
duties and released him into private life.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Fingol


From: Gladstone
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into fragrant spring, and I made ready to carry out 
my imperial orders.  I was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  
Thus did I die, a brave end by any standard.

  Thy humble servant,   Gladstone


