GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT


Kingdom of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1):
  In spring, on the right outside flank, the 218th Legion were arrayed 
against the 121st Garrison.  The 220th Light Cavalry outflanked the 
undermanned enemy and charged in with full force.  On this field, some 
soldiers of the 121st Garrison noticed the presence of an encampment of 
trollops behind their opponents' lines, so they valiantly concentrated their 
efforts to smash through to victory.
  But then the tide of battle reversed.  The army general appeared to 
personally lead the 218th Legion in the front lines, rallying them to a 
truly excellent effort.  The 218th Legion battled with the 121st Garrison 
and managed to make some measure of progress.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 188th Bowmen were blessed by a retinue 
of medicine men sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which aroused them to a 
fanatical zeal.  They faced the 153rd Garrison.  In this match, the 188th 
Bowmen carelessly blundered into a nest of booby traps and lost some 
irreplaceable front-line troops.  The 188th Bowmen battled with the 153rd 
Garrison and fought courageously, but was steadily pushed back.

  In early summer, out on the right outside wing, the 218th Legion were 
aided in the battle by a band of medicine men sent by the League of Pagan 
Clerics, which aroused them to a fanatical zeal.  They were arrayed against 
the 121st Garrison.  The 220th Light Cavalry outflanked the enemy lines and 
charged in with full strength.  On this battleground, the 218th Legion 
audaciously charged their enemy, but became disordered and were thrown back 
by a well-timed, sustained countercharge.  Even so, the 218th Legion battled 
with the 121st Garrison and gradually shoved them back.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 188th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
153rd Garrison.  In this area, the men of the 153rd Garrison encountered 
unpredictable footing and experienced confusion.  The 188th Bowmen fought 
with the 153rd Garrison and the fighting here proved inconclusive.  The 
acting commander withdrew to the Callisto Sea, defeated but not broken.
  In early summer, Odysseus (#97) flew into Bir Nzaran.
  In late summer, Odysseus flew over to Ravenwood.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) ordered an invasion force into the 
adjacent Forest province of Ravenwood, owned by York (#67).  Odysseus (#97) 
commanded the invading armies.  The defending forces were led by York (#67). 
Ravenwood was overrun by Odysseus (#97)'s men in a bloody campaign.
  In fall, Odysseus rode his flying armies into Dirkwood.
  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Jungle province of Dirkwood,
held by the provincial Dragon chieftain.  Odysseus (#97) commanded the 
attacking armies.  The defenders were led by the provincial Dragon chieftain.
Dirkwood was overrun by the forces of Odysseus.

Kingdom of Giovanna d'Arco (#7):
  In spring, Rolando (#55) marched on Moussoro (#1604) with his forces.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in White Magic.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this 
exalted level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 6 in White Magic.  
Your characters of this high level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The White Magician can now use the magic of 
certain Holy Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  At 
any Monastery, Altar or Great Hall, the success chance to cast a White Magic 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in Psychic Magic.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Psychic Magic is 
capped at 3 Action, 2 Combat (however, skill level will still determine who 
attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this high 
level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  PSYCHIC MAGIC- "AUGUR COMBAT" SPELL (abbreviated "AC"):  The Psychic Mage 
performs a powerful augury (forecast), whereby he divines the probable 
outcome of the combat.  The computer will estimate the percentage chance of 
victory, if combat were to occur.  If the plan following the spell is a 
combat-oriented plan, then if the chances are too low for the character's 
courage, he will shirk combat (Coward 80%, Cautious 60%, Brave 40%, Berserk 
20%).  Any encounter plan can be stated after casting this spell.  Usually 
this spell should be the first tactic ordered, when it won't cost you a 
combat round; if it comes later, then the result will be an attempt to flee. 
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 32".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 6 in Psychic Magic.  All 
characters of this exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  PSYCHIC MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The mage is now able to use the magic of 
certain Psychic Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  
At any Tower, Temple or Lost Temple, the success chance to cast a Psychic 
Magic spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is 
applied when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus 
is applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, 
and is not occupied by a monster.


